<% content_for :title, "Privacy · tinyslug" %>
<article class="prose prose-invert mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-lime-300">
  <h1>Privacy by design</h1>
  <p>tinyslug never stores a visitor's raw IP address. When link tracking is enabled, it records a daily rotating digest and coarse request metadata needed for aggregate reports.</p>
  <h2>What link owners can see</h2>
  <p>Reports can include visit counts, daily unique visits, country codes when a trusted local source is configured, referrer hosts, browsers, and device categories. Full referrer URLs and raw user agents are not retained.</p>
  <h2>Your signals are respected</h2>
  <p>Tracking is skipped for Do Not Track, Global Privacy Control, recognized bots, anonymous public-shortener links, and every link whose owner has disabled tracking.</p>
</article>
